# What the mirror pulls from the upstream docroot host. Passed to rsync as a merge file, so
# these are rsync filter rules: first match wins, order matters.
#
# This file is the scope decision, in one place. Editing it changes what R2
# holds; nothing in sync.sh needs to change with it.

# --- checkResults/: keep only the current release and devel ------------------
#
# 2,607,459 files for 38.3 GB -- 70% of every object in the docroot for 8% of
# the bytes. R2 bills per operation, so this directory alone drove the sync
# cost, the wall-clock, and the nightly purge volume.
#
# Keeping 3.23 and 3.24 *-LATEST costs 251,078 files / 3.04 GB and drops
# 2,356,377. Whole-docroot object count falls 3.71M -> 1.35M.
#
# Note the older releases are not "history" in the cheap sense: dated snapshots
# are only 618,420 files. The bulk is each past release's own *-LATEST, 1.65M
# files across 3.13-3.22. Widening this to all versions costs ~1.9M objects, so
# widen deliberately rather than by reflex.
#
# robots.txt already disallows /checkResults/, and these are build telemetry
# rather than published content -- but maintainers do use them, so anything
# dropped here should 404 rather than silently mislead.
+ /checkResults/
# release and devel are symlinks into the version dirs; the Worker resolves
# them from _symlinks.json, so they have to survive the filter.
+ /checkResults/release
+ /checkResults/devel
# The landing page, which is a real file and not an autoindex. Without this the
# `- ***` below drops it and /checkResults/ 404s even though everything it
# links to is present.
+ /checkResults/index.html
+ /checkResults/3.23/
+ /checkResults/3.24/
+ /checkResults/3.23/*-LATEST/***
+ /checkResults/3.24/*-LATEST/***
- /checkResults/***

# --- abandoned staging in the live docroot -----------------------------------
#
# 6.1 GB / 2,701 files. The name is upstream's. Contains symlinks pointing at
# absolute paths under the live docroot/, so it never resolved cleanly anyway.
- /LoriTempToRemove/***

# --- rsync/filesystem noise --------------------------------------------------
#
# Unanchored: there is a lost+found under packages/ as well as at the root, and
# the rsync user cannot read either, so anchoring to / just moves the
# permission-denied error rather than removing it.
- lost+found/
- .*.??????

# Seven 2013 course-material files are unreadable by the rsync user
# (help/course-materials/2013/EMBOBGI/...). Deliberately NOT excluded: they
# return 403 from the live site too, so Apache cannot read them either. The
# mirror loses nothing, and leaving them to error keeps the condition visible
# rather than silently normalising an upstream permissions bug. Reported in
# the upstream-findings issue.
